{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetNonzero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetNonzero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGram","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGramRankOne","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramNondegenerate","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCarrierEquiv","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_rank_one_agrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_rank_one_agrees","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetNonzero.lean#L80-L96","doc":"**Cross-check at the one rank computed by hand.**\n\n`twGram_det_rank_one` gives `det (twGram K Q 1) = (1 + Q) ^ 2` by direct evaluation of the\nfour Markov-trace entries.  At `Q = q ^ 2` its non-vanishing is `q ^ 4 ≠ 1`, which is exactly\nwhat `NotRootOfUnity q` supplies — so this reaches the same conclusion as\n`twGram_det_ne_zero` at `n = 1` by a completely different route (an explicit `2 × 2`\ndeterminant, rather than Wedderburn plus the trace-form radical).\n\nKept as a regression: an error in either route would show up as a disagreement here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_of_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_of_sq","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetNonzero.lean#L71-L78","doc":"**The same at an Iwahori parameter `Q` given as a square.**  The shape a caller holding\n`Q` wants, once it can exhibit a square root — mirroring\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.isSemisimpleRing_iwahoriHecke_of_sq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetNonzero.lean#L56-L69","doc":"**`det(twGram) ≠ 0` at every rank**, over any characteristic-zero field, for `q ≠ 0` not a\nroot of unity.\n\nComposes two isomorphisms — `skeinIwahoriEquiv` (Iwahori at `q ^ 2` is the skein algebra at\n`q`) and `heckeWedderburn` (the skein algebra is a product of matrix algebras) — and feeds the\nresult to the converse Gram criterion.  No determinant is evaluated anywhere in the proof. ","signatureChunk":0}]}